# CR-026: docker/compose.yaml's build context is the monorepo root
# (`context: ../../..`), not this package — Docker only reads a plain
# `.dockerignore` from the CONTEXT root, and there is none at the repo root.
# `../.dockerignore` (packages/flight/.dockerignore) documents itself as
# inert at that depth for the same reason. Without this file, `COPY
# packages/flight packages/flight` in ./Dockerfile pulled in
# packages/flight/.env verbatim — the file this same compose.yaml's env_file
# directive tells operators to create for their provider keys — baking
# secrets into an image layer, along with node_modules/dist/.turbo from the
# host.
#
# BuildKit resolves a per-Dockerfile ignore file named `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# placed in the SAME DIRECTORY as the Dockerfile it applies to (this is a
# documented Docker convention, independent of the context root), so this
# file covers ./Dockerfile without needing anything outside packages/flight.
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root (the
# monorepo root), hence the leading `**/`.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
.git
